            <div xml:id="d370">

                <pb facs="0562" n="472" xml:id="pg472"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/12777: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1934-08-03T15:00:00+08:00">August 3, 1934—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received August 3—9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>337. Reference the Legation’s telegram No. 334 of August 2, 5 p.m., Commander in
                    Chief of the United States Asiatic Fleet informs me that he has ordered U. S. S.
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Sacramento</hi> to proceed immediately to Pagoda
                    Anchorage. Foochow informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
